E CRAFT; TOTAL PROFIT IS\n> THE BACKEND'S TOTAL FOR EVERY CRAFT IT COUNTED. THE TABLE SCROLLS SIDEWAYS\n> INSIDE ITS OWN REGION WHEN THE COLUMNS DO NOT FIT; THE PAGE AROUND IT DOES NOT.\n\nTHE INTERACTION SHOULD BE UNDERSTANDABLE THROUGH THE UI ITSELF.\n\nACCESSIBILITY BEHAVIOR SUCH AS KEYBOARD-OPERABLE ROW SELECTION MUST REMAIN,\nBUT IT DOES NOT REQUIRE PERMANENT INSTRUCTIONAL PROSE ON THE PAGE.\n\nCOLUMN HEADINGS AND LAYOUT SHOULD COMMUNICATE THE DISTINCTION BETWEEN PER-CRAFT\nAND TOTAL VALUES WITHOUT REQUIRING THIS PARAGRAPH.\n\n---\n\n#### REMOVE DISPLAY-LIMIT EXPLANATION\n\nREMOVE THE DYNAMICALLY DISPLAYED EXPLANATORY TEXT SUCH AS:\n\n> THE DISPLAY MAXIMUM OF 250 IS HOLDING BACK 63 FURTHER MATCHING RECIPES.\n> SWITCH ON SHOW ALL MATCHING RECIPES TO LIST EVERY ONE OF THEM.\n\nTHE MAXIMUM-RESULT CONTROL AND `SHOW ALL` OPTION SHOULD BE SUFFICIENTLY CLEAR\nWITHOUT AN EXPLANATORY PARAGRAPH.\n\nA COMPACT COUNT SUCH AS:\n\n`250 OF 313 RECIPES`\n\nMAY BE SHOWN IF USEFUL, BUT IT SHOULD NOT BECOME ANOTHER INSTRUCTIONAL BLOCK.\n\n---\n\n#### REMOVE RESULT-FILTER EXPLANATION\n\nREMOVE THE FOLLOWING TEXT:\n\n> THESE CHANGE WHICH OF THE CALCULATED RECIPES ARE LISTED BELOW. THEY NEVER\n> RECALCULATE ANYTHING, NEVER CHANGE THE CALCULATION CONTROLS ABOVE, AND NEVER\n> CHANGE HOW FAR THE BACKEND SIMULATED EACH RECIPE.\n\nTHE DISTINCTION BETWEEN CALCULATION CONTROLS AND DISPLAY FILTERS SHOULD INSTEAD\nBE COMMUNICATED THROUGH THEIR GROUPING AND LABELS.\n\nTHIS BEHAVIOR MUST STILL REMAIN TRUE EVEN THOUGH THE EXPLANATORY PARAGRAPH IS\nREMOVED.\n\n---\n\n#### REMOVE REDUNDANT TRADING POST UNIT-PRICE EXPLANATION\n\nFROM THE SELECTED-RESULT DETAIL PANEL REMOVE TEXT SUCH AS:\n\n> EACH IS THE PRICE OF A SINGLE ITEM. ONE CRAFT OF THIS RECIPE PRODUCES 1.\n\nTHE TRADING POST UNIT PRICE SHOULD INSTEAD HAVE A CONCISE, SELF-EXPLANATORY\nLABEL, FOR EXAMPLE:\n\n`TRADING POST PRICE / ITEM`\n\nOR ANOTHER CLEAR EQUIVALENT.\n\nRECIPE OUTPUT QUANTITY BELONGS WITH THE RECIPE/CRAFTING INFORMATION AND S